From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, shcore, explorer: a window's property store is kept, and AppUserModelIDs group taskbar buttons

SHGetPropertyStoreForWindow returned a store that kept nothing: GetValue,
GetCount and GetAt returned E_NOTIMPL and SetValue returned S_OK and
dropped the value. Programs that give a window its own AppUserModelID
(Chromium's installed web apps, Java and Python programs that share one
executable, Electron, programs with several top-level identities) had it
ignored, and the taskbar grouped buttons by executable alone. Another
process could not see a process's explicit ID either.

- A window's properties are the window's: shell32 keeps them in a
  volatile key per window (HKCU\Software\Wine\Shell\WindowProperties\
  <hwnd>), a value per property holding its VARTYPE and data, so every
  process reads what was set; the taskbar removes the key with the window.
  Strings, integers, booleans, floating point, FILETIME and CLSID values
  are kept; VT_EMPTY takes a property away; an AppUserModelID over 128
  characters is refused (E_INVALIDARG); there is no store for a window
  that is not there.
- SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID also publishes the ID (with the
  process's start time, against reused process ids).
- The taskbar groups by AppUserModelID -- the window's, else its
  program's explicit one -- before the program's file, as Windows does:
  one program's windows with different IDs are separate buttons, another
  program with the same ID joins them. It reads them again when a window's
  ID changes. "Open another" and the button menu's program entry run the
  window's System.AppUserModel.RelaunchCommand when it has one;
  System.AppUserModel.PreventPinning takes "Pin to taskbar" away.

Wine's shell32 appbar tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/winappid-gate.sh (Xvfb, the shell's desktop, buttons combined:
the store read back here and from another process, the buttons counted as
IDs are given, changed, shared with another process and taken away).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_GROUP_BY_EXE (programs/explorer/systray.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_PROCESS_AUMID_SHARED (shcore/main.c),
SG_MUTANT_PROPSTORE_ANY_WINDOW (shell32/shell32_main.c).
---
--- a/dlls/shcore/main.c
+++ b/dlls/shcore/main.c
@@ -302,6 +302,26 @@ static CRITICAL_SECTION_DEBUG aumid_cs_debug =
 };
 static CRITICAL_SECTION aumid_cs = { &aumid_cs_debug, -1, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
 
+/* Stained Glass OS (1640): the taskbar groups a program's windows by its
+ * explicit ID, so it is published where the taskbar reads it: a volatile key
+ * per process, HKCU\Software\Wine\Shell\ProcessAppIds\<pid>, with the
+ * process's start time to tell a reused process id from it */
+static void publish_process_aumid( const WCHAR *appid )
+{
+    FILETIME created, exited, kernel, user;
+    WCHAR path[64];
+    ULONGLONG start;
+    HKEY key;
+
+    if (!GetProcessTimes( GetCurrentProcess(), &created, &exited, &kernel, &user )) return;
+    start = ((ULONGLONG)created.dwHighDateTime << 32) | created.dwLowDateTime;
+    swprintf( path, ARRAY_SIZE(path), L"Software\\Wine\\Shell\\ProcessAppIds\\%lu", GetCurrentProcessId() );
+    if (RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, path, 0, NULL, REG_OPTION_VOLATILE, KEY_WRITE, NULL, &key, NULL )) return;
+    RegSetValueExW( key, L"Id", 0, REG_SZ, (const BYTE *)appid, (wcslen( appid ) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+    RegSetValueExW( key, L"Started", 0, REG_QWORD, (const BYTE *)&start, sizeof(start) );
+    RegCloseKey( key );
+}
+
 HRESULT WINAPI SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(const WCHAR *appid)
 {
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_AUMID
@@ -316,6 +336,9 @@ HRESULT WINAPI SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID(const WCHAR *appid)
     free( explicit_aumid );
     explicit_aumid = copy;
     LeaveCriticalSection( &aumid_cs );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_PROCESS_AUMID_SHARED
+    publish_process_aumid( appid );
+#endif
     return S_OK;
 #else
     FIXME("%s: stub\n", debugstr_w(appid));
--- a/dlls/shell32/shell32_main.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shell32_main.c
@@ -704,10 +704,34 @@ VOID WINAPI Printers_UnregisterWindow(HANDLE hClassPidl, HWND hwnd)
     FIXME("(%p, %p) stub!\n", hClassPidl, hwnd);
